Package: v4l2-request-va-driver
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libva2 (>= 2.24)
Enhances: libva2
Provides: va-driver
Description: VA-API driver for V4L2 stateless (Request API) video decoders
 A libva backend that drives the Linux V4L2 stateless decoder interface
 (Media Request API), as found on Rockchip (rkvdec, Hantro, AV1 VPU),
 Allwinner (cedrus) and other SoCs whose GPU has no video engine. VA-API
 applications - Firefox, Chromium, mpv, FFmpeg, GStreamer va - can then use
 the hardware decoders for MPEG-2, H.264, HEVC, VP8, VP9 and AV1, with
 decoded frames exported as dma-bufs (no copies).
 .
 The package also installs panthor_drv_video.so and panfrost_drv_video.so
 links, so that libva picks this driver for the Arm Mali render nodes
 (which have no video engine) without LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME.
